1
00:00:01,334 --> 00:00:02,460
"Previously on The Mentalist"

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,505
Lisbon, I just want you to know
I'm okay.

3
00:00:07,381 --> 00:00:08,424
"And I'm gonna miss you."

4
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:14,138
- Patrick.
- Kim.

5
00:00:14,555 --> 00:00:16,641
Thank you for this.
I needed the company.

6
00:00:16,807 --> 00:00:17,934
I'm here to make you
an offer.

7
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:20,770
The Bureau is willing to drop
all of the charges against you

8
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:22,063
if you come
and work for us.

9
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:23,981
"You are on U.S. soil now."

10
00:00:24,148 --> 00:00:26,359
This is the deal.

11
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:28,236
- Take it or leave it.
- I leave it.

12
00:00:28,486 --> 00:00:30,446
They conceded
to all your demands.

13
00:00:30,571 --> 00:00:32,907
Every single one.
How did you do it?

14
00:00:33,115 --> 00:00:35,826
Well, remember that thumb drive
we found in Bertram's wine cellar?

15
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:37,203
The encrypted database.

16
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:40,581
"It's a list of Blake Association members.
I used it as leverage."

17
00:00:40,831 --> 00:00:43,459
- But we never broke the encryption.
- Yeah, F.B.I. doesn't know that.

18
00:00:54,470 --> 00:00:57,515
Got a desk ready for you.
You can work right back here.

19
00:00:57,682 --> 00:00:58,724
Eh, I don't need a desk.

20
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:01,561
- Really? You work standing up?
- Lying down.

21
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,021
- I need a couch.
- Really?

22
00:01:04,146 --> 00:01:07,984
Really. Opens the mind.
That's why shrinks have you lie down.

23
00:01:08,359 --> 00:01:10,528
I wouldn't know.
You can't have a sofa here.

24
00:01:12,071 --> 00:01:13,948
- You've never been to a shrink?
- No.

25
00:01:14,615 --> 00:01:16,867
Interesting. That's a lie.
We'll come back to that.

26
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,661
Why? Why can't I have a couch?

27
00:01:18,869 --> 00:01:21,914
Only grade 3 employees and above
can have sofas.

28
00:01:22,164 --> 00:01:25,918
Sofas, couches, potatoes, "potatoes."

29
00:01:26,168 --> 00:01:28,212
- Uh, what grade am I?
- You're a consultant.

30
00:01:28,337 --> 00:01:29,422
You're not in the grading system.

31
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:31,132
- What grade are you?
- Four.

32
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:33,259
You can apply for an ergonomic
chair if you have back issues

33
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:34,844
but you'll have to get
a doctor's note.

34
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:37,638
No. I asked for a couch,
and Abbott, your boss

35
00:01:37,763 --> 00:01:38,806
said I could have a couch.

36
00:01:38,931 --> 00:01:42,059
You can have a sofa.
You just can't have it here.

37
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,186
No couch, no me.

38
00:01:44,312 --> 00:01:45,771
Okay, you don't understand
the deal here.

39
00:01:45,896 --> 00:01:47,523
You don't get to make the rules.

40
00:01:47,648 --> 00:01:50,109
Yes, I do,
and you've already seen that I do.

41
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:53,988
Why do you say that you've
never been to a shrink?

42
00:01:55,239 --> 00:01:56,282
What are you ashamed of?

43
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,202
I'm sorry
that I deceived you, Patrick.

44
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:02,496
- Truly. Good.
- But you didn't deceive me.

45
00:02:03,122 --> 00:02:04,206
I'm glad you feel that way.

46
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:07,293
I didn't intend to get so involved.

47
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:11,088
I was meant to confirm your identity
and keep tabs on you.

48
00:02:11,672 --> 00:02:14,300
And then we started talking,
and I...

49
00:02:18,095 --> 00:02:20,222
Whatever. I'm sorry.

50
00:02:20,806 --> 00:02:23,225
And I will attempt
to make it up to you

51
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:25,519
by being as honest
as possible in the future.

52
00:02:25,686 --> 00:02:27,355
Do you always mask your guilt
with anger?

53
00:02:29,106 --> 00:02:31,025
There's nothing in my life
that I'm ashamed of.

54
00:02:31,567 --> 00:02:32,610
But it is my life

55
00:02:32,735 --> 00:02:35,529
and whether I have been
to a shrink or I haven't

56
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,323
that's not your business.

57
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:40,409
Uh, this is the conference
room, obviously.

58
00:02:40,534 --> 00:02:42,161
The break room is through here.

59
00:02:42,286 --> 00:02:43,621
What did you see
a shrink about?

60
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:46,832
Okay.

61
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:51,796
- I will get you a couch.
- Hmm. Good.

62
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:54,674
I like the club style,
but obviously bigger.

63
00:02:55,007 --> 00:02:57,885
Worn leather, something I can
really snuggle into, you know?

64
00:02:58,010 --> 00:02:59,804
Just like the one I had
at the CBI.

65
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:03,265
Fischer. Saddle up.
We're going to Corpus Christi.

66
00:03:03,766 --> 00:03:05,434
Five DEA agents were murdered.

67
00:03:05,601 --> 00:03:08,479
- Five?
- Five. Let's go.

68
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:23,202
There's three different
caliber casings

69
00:03:23,327 --> 00:03:25,204
so there were three shooters,
maybe more.

70
00:03:31,752 --> 00:03:33,129
These people never knew
what hit 'em.

71
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:52,648
Well, they found
the security camera.

72
00:03:52,773 --> 00:03:53,899
It was hidden in the clock.

73
00:03:58,070 --> 00:03:59,530
Got another one here
hidden in a lamp.

74
00:04:02,158 --> 00:04:03,325
They knew what they were
looking for.

75
00:04:09,498 --> 00:04:11,709
One of the agents survived
the initial shooting.

76
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:13,085
See the streaks of blood?

77
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:20,551
He was trying to crawl to safety
when he was killed.

78
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:24,138
Clean job.
No witnesses, no footage.

79
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:30,519
Why is there a mirror
in this room

80
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:33,731
and why is it set so high
on the wall?

81
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:41,822
- Another camera.
- Et voilà.

82
00:04:57,252 --> 00:05:00,464
Listen. I know who did this.
I know it.

83
00:05:00,798 --> 00:05:03,717
What agent Higgins means
is the DEA has strong reason

84
00:05:03,842 --> 00:05:06,220
to believe a Corpus Christi
narcotics organization

85
00:05:06,345 --> 00:05:09,181
is behind the murders,
the Gulf Coast Ring.

86
00:05:09,389 --> 00:05:12,100
- Why would they want to do this?
- Retaliation.

87
00:05:12,893 --> 00:05:15,187
Last month, we took
100 kilos off the ring

88
00:05:15,312 --> 00:05:17,147
and shot and killed
one of their lieutenants.

89
00:05:17,272 --> 00:05:18,941
We've been hearing
they wanted payback.

90
00:05:19,191 --> 00:05:22,069
{\an8}I.A. investigated.
It was a clean shooting.

91
00:05:22,194 --> 00:05:24,154
{\an8}We first caught wind
of the ring two years ago.

92
00:05:24,488 --> 00:05:26,323
{\an8}They're disciplined,
they're organized

93
00:05:26,448 --> 00:05:27,491
{\an8}and highly secretive.

94
00:05:27,908 --> 00:05:29,034
{\an8}The bust we made
a few weeks ago

95
00:05:29,159 --> 00:05:30,911
{\an8}was the first dent we made
in their operations.

96
00:05:31,161 --> 00:05:34,081
{\an8}But they still control virtually
all drug flow into Corpus Christi.

97
00:05:34,373 --> 00:05:35,958
{\an8}Where were you
when the shootings occurred?

98
00:05:36,458 --> 00:05:37,501
{\an8}Was home.

99
00:05:37,793 --> 00:05:39,378
I was on surveillance late
the night before.

100
00:05:39,545 --> 00:05:41,380
Who runs the Gulf Coast Ring?

101
00:05:44,091 --> 00:05:45,133
{\an8}We don't know.

102
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:46,677
But we do have a profile.

103
00:05:47,594 --> 00:05:50,973
{\an8}We think this Mr. X is an intelligent
and disciplined businessman

104
00:05:51,098 --> 00:05:53,267
{\an8}mostly likely using
a legitimate front as cover.

105
00:05:53,392 --> 00:05:54,893
- Hiding in plain sight.
- That's right.

106
00:05:55,853 --> 00:05:56,937
Look, most of these guys

107
00:05:57,354 --> 00:05:58,730
{\an8}they want you to know
who they are.

108
00:05:58,856 --> 00:06:00,566
{\an8}It drives them.
But this one

109
00:06:01,483 --> 00:06:02,609
it's like he doesn't have an ego.

110
00:06:02,776 --> 00:06:05,487
- Well, that's odd, isn't it?
- What's that?

111
00:06:05,612 --> 00:06:07,656
{\an8}Well, well you said that Mr. X
is disciplined.

112
00:06:07,781 --> 00:06:09,199
{\an8}Uh, I would think that

113
00:06:09,825 --> 00:06:12,619
{\an8}shooting five DEA agents
is anything but disciplined.

114
00:06:14,288 --> 00:06:15,330
Who do you have in mind?

115
00:06:16,957 --> 00:06:18,292
{\an8}There's a few possibilities.

116
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:21,503
Hector Ruiz.

117
00:06:22,212 --> 00:06:24,756
{\an8}A real estate developer
based in Corpus Christi.

118
00:06:24,882 --> 00:06:26,717
{\an8}But he has dealings
throughout Texas.

119
00:06:27,968 --> 00:06:30,554
{\an8}Francisco Perez,
a.k.a. Paco

120
00:06:30,762 --> 00:06:33,223
a Colombian national
with ties to a drug cartel.

121
00:06:33,557 --> 00:06:34,850
{\an8}Now we know
he's in the city now

122
00:06:34,975 --> 00:06:36,310
{\an8}but we're still not sure why.

123
00:06:37,394 --> 00:06:39,062
{\an8}He's only been in the states
a few months.

124
00:06:40,522 --> 00:06:43,442
Michael Ellis.
He runs a financial group.

125
00:06:43,609 --> 00:06:46,194
It's mostly private equity,
but some international business.

126
00:06:46,695 --> 00:06:48,614
{\an8}He's been investigated
for tax fraud

127
00:06:48,739 --> 00:06:51,783
{\an8}SEC violations.
But nothing's stuck.

128
00:06:51,992 --> 00:06:54,745
- Um, who? Who? who's this?
- It's Richie Vargas.

129
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:56,496
He's the ring member
who got killed in the bust.

130
00:06:56,622 --> 00:06:58,624
- Yeah, no, the woman.
- Oh.

131
00:06:59,499 --> 00:07:01,376
It's Krystal Markham,
Vargas' girlfriend.

132
00:07:01,752 --> 00:07:03,712
Hm. You know where we can
find her?

133
00:07:04,713 --> 00:07:06,256
{\an8}Uh, we've questioned her in the past.

134
00:07:06,381 --> 00:07:07,674
{\an8}Few times.
She wasn't much help.

135
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:09,843
{\an8}Do you know where
we can find her?

136
00:07:11,428 --> 00:07:12,471
"Shut that door!"

137
00:07:13,138 --> 00:07:15,390
"Wylie, you get anything from
the DEA footage we sent you?"

138
00:07:15,515 --> 00:07:17,184
As a matter of fact, yes.

139
00:07:17,309 --> 00:07:19,811
{\an8}- IDs on all three gunmen.
- That was fast.

140
00:07:19,978 --> 00:07:21,688
{\an8}Uh, Once I pulled clean photos
from the footage

141
00:07:21,813 --> 00:07:24,149
it was just a matter of running
a facial recognition program.

142
00:07:24,274 --> 00:07:25,734
All three were
in the federal database.

143
00:07:25,901 --> 00:07:28,320
- Well, who are they?
- According to Corpus Christi P.D.

144
00:07:28,487 --> 00:07:29,529
they're local street criminals.

145
00:07:29,655 --> 00:07:31,156
Nothing to do
with the Gulf Coast Ring.

146
00:07:31,281 --> 00:07:32,866
Maybe the DEA was wrong.

147
00:07:32,991 --> 00:07:34,701
{\an8}Or maybe the ring
freelanced out the shooting.

148
00:07:35,035 --> 00:07:37,204
{\an8}Addresses are current,
but they're not gonna help.

149
00:07:37,329 --> 00:07:39,790
{\an8}Local police checked them out.
Gunmen are long gone.

150
00:07:39,915 --> 00:07:42,376
{\an8}So we have to wait for a hit
on the BOLO. I hate that.

151
00:07:42,501 --> 00:07:43,710
You wanna take a drive
down to Corpus Christi?

152
00:07:43,835 --> 00:07:44,878
Yeah, let's go.

153
00:08:03,730 --> 00:08:05,774
{\an8}Did you listen to the audio
on the DEA surveillance video?

154
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,442
Yeah. Why?

155
00:08:07,651 --> 00:08:09,653
{\an8}Well, you couldn't see the gunmen's car
but you could hear its engine.

156
00:08:10,278 --> 00:08:11,321
So?

157
00:08:12,072 --> 00:08:13,115
{\an8}So maybe we can use that.

158
00:08:14,032 --> 00:08:15,117
That's a fantastic idea.

159
00:08:15,742 --> 00:08:19,204
Every engine model has its own
unique audio signature.

160
00:08:19,329 --> 00:08:21,081
{\an8}If we can analyze the gunmen's

161
00:08:21,206 --> 00:08:23,709
{\an8}and compare it to known
engine signatures

162
00:08:24,292 --> 00:08:25,836
we might just have a match.

163
00:08:26,044 --> 00:08:27,963
- Great. Call me if you get something.
- You got it.

164
00:08:28,130 --> 00:08:29,589
- He can do it?
- Yeah.

165
00:08:30,173 --> 00:08:32,634
- F.B.I.
- Yeah.

166
00:08:45,022 --> 00:08:46,064
"He's there right now?"

167
00:08:49,609 --> 00:08:50,652
Krystal Markham?

168
00:08:51,778 --> 00:08:53,697
- Yes?
- Agent Fischer with the F.B.I.

169
00:08:53,822 --> 00:08:54,906
this is Patrick Jane.

170
00:08:55,032 --> 00:08:58,452
We'd like to ask you a few questions
about recent shooting at a DEA office.

171
00:08:58,618 --> 00:08:59,828
I don't know anything about it.

172
00:09:00,412 --> 00:09:02,873
Five DEA agents
lost their lives, ma'am.

173
00:09:03,915 --> 00:09:06,835
Oh, yes. I remember now.
It was on the news. Terrible.

174
00:09:08,211 --> 00:09:09,671
- What about it?
- Well, some people think

175
00:09:09,796 --> 00:09:11,089
the Gulf Coast Ring did it.

176
00:09:11,256 --> 00:09:13,717
revenge for the death of your boyfriend
Richie Vargas.

177
00:09:13,884 --> 00:09:17,262
- Richie wasn't my boyfriend.
- No? Uh, what would you call him?

178
00:09:17,471 --> 00:09:19,639
A friend. A good friend.

179
00:09:19,890 --> 00:09:21,892
And I'm very sad that he is gone.

180
00:09:22,434 --> 00:09:24,644
- Um, he was a sweet guy.
- He was a gangster.

181
00:09:24,936 --> 00:09:26,188
- I didn't know that.
- No?

182
00:09:26,772 --> 00:09:28,148
I never asked him
what he did for a living.

183
00:09:28,273 --> 00:09:30,442
That can be a rude
question, you know?

184
00:09:30,901 --> 00:09:31,943
Excuse me.

185
00:09:34,154 --> 00:09:36,198
- May I go?
- Uh, yeah. Of, of course.

186
00:09:36,323 --> 00:09:38,366
Um, but first, could I...
Could I get your phone number?

187
00:09:38,658 --> 00:09:40,077
I told you
I don't know anything.

188
00:09:40,285 --> 00:09:41,328
I believe you.

189
00:09:41,453 --> 00:09:43,371
That's not why I'm asking
for your number.

190
00:09:45,207 --> 00:09:46,833
I'm a little out of practice.
I'm sorry.

191
00:09:47,292 --> 00:09:48,335
It's been a while.

192
00:09:49,503 --> 00:09:51,546
- Oh. You want my number?
- Yes

193
00:09:51,671 --> 00:09:53,965
then I could possibly call it
and maybe we could...

194
00:09:54,674 --> 00:09:58,512
Wow. I don't know.
I never, um...

195
00:09:59,262 --> 00:10:00,889
Uh, that was Wylie
back at the office.

196
00:10:01,014 --> 00:10:02,265
He'd ID'd the gunmen's vehicle.

197
00:10:02,390 --> 00:10:04,559
Late '60s Chevy Impala.
There are three in the area

198
00:10:04,684 --> 00:10:06,061
but none of them's registered
to the gunmen.

199
00:10:06,186 --> 00:10:07,521
Do we know
where the three are?

200
00:10:07,729 --> 00:10:09,564
One of them's in downtown
Corpus Christi.

201
00:10:09,689 --> 00:10:11,358
Second was spotted near
the warehouse district

202
00:10:11,483 --> 00:10:14,486
and the third is in Bella Vista,
so we have our day cut out for us.

203
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,155
Thanks for your time,
Miss Markham.

204
00:10:20,075 --> 00:10:21,118
Could you give us a moment?

205
00:10:24,329 --> 00:10:26,748
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

206
00:10:28,166 --> 00:10:30,335
So you, you were, you were saying
you've never...

207
00:10:30,585 --> 00:10:31,878
I never dated a cop.

208
00:10:32,629 --> 00:10:34,464
Well, nor will you now.
I'm not a cop.

209
00:10:35,507 --> 00:10:38,718
- Well, what are you then?
- I'm not a what, I'm a who.

210
00:10:39,261 --> 00:10:42,389
And I'd be happy to tell you
which who over dinner.

211
00:10:55,944 --> 00:10:57,070
Thank you. I'll call you.

212
00:10:58,196 --> 00:10:59,239
Maybe I'll answer.

213
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:10,709
- Did you just ask her out?
- Yep.

214
00:11:11,626 --> 00:11:13,879
Good for you, I guess.

215
00:11:16,089 --> 00:11:17,966
- I'm surprised.
- Hm?

216
00:11:20,093 --> 00:11:21,636
I wouldn't have thought
that she was your type.

217
00:11:22,304 --> 00:11:23,805
She thinks the Impala
we're looking for

218
00:11:23,930 --> 00:11:25,182
is in the warehouse district.

219
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:28,351
- She does? How can you tell?
- I can tell.

220
00:11:29,811 --> 00:11:31,938
Oh. Oh, you think...

221
00:11:32,105 --> 00:11:33,982
You think she knows more
than she's saying.

222
00:11:34,107 --> 00:11:35,901
That's, that's why
you asked her out.

223
00:11:36,318 --> 00:11:39,237
No. I asked her out 'cause
she's just my type.

224
00:11:40,113 --> 00:11:41,656
- She say yes?
- She did.

225
00:11:42,824 --> 00:11:44,576
Huh. Huh.

226
00:11:45,744 --> 00:11:48,079
She may be your type
but you don't seem like hers.

227
00:11:48,747 --> 00:11:50,040
Nah, she was happy
I asked her.

228
00:11:50,957 --> 00:11:52,709
Once I convinced her
I wasn't a cop.

229
00:11:53,251 --> 00:11:54,294
Are we gonna go anywhere?

230
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:03,929
"Hey, Cho. Fischer thinks the gunmen
are holed up in the marina warehouse."

231
00:12:04,596 --> 00:12:06,056
"I'm texting you the address now."

232
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:15,398
- This our car?
- Yep.

233
00:12:26,451 --> 00:12:28,453
Okay, you two take the side
and the rear of the warehouse.

234
00:12:29,037 --> 00:12:30,080
You're with us.

235
00:12:36,628 --> 00:12:37,837
Krystal, it's Patrick Jane.

236
00:12:38,171 --> 00:12:39,589
Give me a call
when you get a chance.

237
00:12:39,923 --> 00:12:41,466
I wanna know if you wanna meet me
for dinner tonight.

238
00:13:04,990 --> 00:13:06,032
Clear.

239
00:13:07,826 --> 00:13:09,369
- Clear.
- Let's check the back.

240
00:13:11,830 --> 00:13:12,872
"Clear."

241
00:13:15,625 --> 00:13:16,668
"Clear on the side."

242
00:13:21,131 --> 00:13:22,173
Clear.

243
00:13:23,216 --> 00:13:24,884
- Wow.
- Yeah.

244
00:13:25,885 --> 00:13:26,928
Think we got something.

245
00:13:27,304 --> 00:13:28,346
"I'm coming in."

246
00:13:36,479 --> 00:13:37,522
Found the gunmen.

247
00:13:41,901 --> 00:13:42,944
Ooh.

248
00:13:47,282 --> 00:13:48,325
Hey, Krystal.

249
00:13:49,367 --> 00:13:50,618
No, no. Now's a good time.

250
00:13:51,619 --> 00:13:52,662
So how about dinner tonight?

251
00:13:54,122 --> 00:13:55,540
Great. Great.

252
00:13:55,999 --> 00:13:57,542
Let's say 8:00. Um...

253
00:13:58,001 --> 00:14:00,003
Shall I pick you up, or...
or meet you there?

254
00:14:01,963 --> 00:14:03,631
Awesome. Look forward to it.

255
00:14:13,473 --> 00:14:15,350
So all three victims
were killed in the same fashion.

256
00:14:15,975 --> 00:14:17,101
Their throats were slit first.

257
00:14:17,226 --> 00:14:18,519
That accounts
for the amount of blood.

258
00:14:20,146 --> 00:14:21,397
And then for good measure,
I suppose

259
00:14:21,522 --> 00:14:23,566
they were re-shot in the head.
Close range.

260
00:14:24,317 --> 00:14:25,651
Someone sure wanted
these men dead.

261
00:14:26,402 --> 00:14:28,029
You work any cartel
murders before?

262
00:14:28,321 --> 00:14:30,073
Enough to know this fits
their MO.

263
00:14:30,406 --> 00:14:32,575
- Just what I was thinking.
- Got it.

264
00:14:32,825 --> 00:14:34,410
Gunmen dead, justice served.

265
00:14:34,535 --> 00:14:35,745
Are we gonna be here
much longer?

266
00:14:35,870 --> 00:14:37,789
'Cause I got some plans.

267
00:14:38,164 --> 00:14:39,916
Here we go.
Got a burner phone.

268
00:14:41,376 --> 00:14:43,461
- No numbers in the contacts.
- Call log?

269
00:14:44,128 --> 00:14:46,506
Six calls made,
all in the past three days

270
00:14:46,631 --> 00:14:48,049
- all to the same number.
- Try it.

271
00:14:51,761 --> 00:14:52,804
Disconnected.

272
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:56,474
The phone company says the number
was disconnected yesterday.

273
00:14:56,933 --> 00:14:57,975
Who was it registered to?

274
00:15:01,187 --> 00:15:05,149
Frank Price, which just so happens
to be a known alias of...

275
00:15:06,234 --> 00:15:08,111
Francisco "Paco" Perez.

276
00:15:08,444 --> 00:15:10,238
34, Colombian national.

277
00:15:10,822 --> 00:15:14,117
And has strong family ties
to the Espedes cartel in Bogotá.

278
00:15:14,325 --> 00:15:16,577
You said he's been in the states
the last three months.

279
00:15:16,953 --> 00:15:18,579
- Doing what?
- I'm not sure.

280
00:15:19,205 --> 00:15:21,457
- Before that?
- Again, not sure.

281
00:15:21,582 --> 00:15:23,251
Colombian records aren't
what they could be.

282
00:15:23,709 --> 00:15:27,255
- And you like him for our Mr. X?
- Yeah. Always have.

283
00:15:28,214 --> 00:15:30,133
The other suspects,
Ruiz and Ellis?

284
00:15:30,258 --> 00:15:33,261
They fit the profile,
but, uh, I've met 'em

285
00:15:33,594 --> 00:15:34,637
talked to 'em.

286
00:15:34,887 --> 00:15:36,681
Running a drug ring? Murder?

287
00:15:37,515 --> 00:15:38,891
I don't see them
as being capable.

288
00:15:39,267 --> 00:15:40,977
Then why not just move in
on Perez?

289
00:15:41,185 --> 00:15:43,146
He was a hard sell
to my supervisors.

290
00:15:44,272 --> 00:15:46,941
Our intel tells us that Perez
is a middleman

291
00:15:47,066 --> 00:15:49,402
between the cartel
and the Corpus Christi drug ring

292
00:15:49,777 --> 00:15:52,530
not the man in charge.
But for my money

293
00:15:53,781 --> 00:15:54,824
He's the guy.

294
00:15:55,199 --> 00:15:56,868
We're having a hard time
tracking Perez down.

295
00:15:57,577 --> 00:15:58,870
What else can you
tell us about him?

296
00:16:00,663 --> 00:16:01,706
Not much.

297
00:16:02,123 --> 00:16:03,541
Perez keeps a low profile.

298
00:16:05,126 --> 00:16:07,503
To be honest, I'm surprised
he left behind a burner cell.

299
00:16:08,004 --> 00:16:09,922
It's not like him.
It's sloppy.

300
00:16:17,722 --> 00:16:18,764
Thank you.

301
00:16:18,973 --> 00:16:20,016
Sure. Thanks.

302
00:16:24,228 --> 00:16:25,271
Thank you.

303
00:16:30,151 --> 00:16:31,319
Are you gonna tell me
who you are?

304
00:16:31,986 --> 00:16:33,738
Oh, no, that was just
a sales pitch.

305
00:16:33,863 --> 00:16:37,241
I never, uh, really tell anyone
who I actually am.

306
00:16:38,659 --> 00:16:40,077
That's why we're
so well-matched.

307
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:41,913
I think you're the same.

308
00:16:43,539 --> 00:16:44,874
- You think?
- Well, uh...

309
00:16:44,999 --> 00:16:47,502
there's a real Krystal
that you don't let anybody see.

310
00:16:48,419 --> 00:16:50,922
Underneath the glamour
and the smiles, uh

311
00:16:51,881 --> 00:16:54,592
there's someone that's honest
and strong and down to earth.

312
00:16:57,553 --> 00:16:58,596
Maybe.

313
00:16:58,971 --> 00:17:00,264
Well, that's the Krystal
I wanna meet.

314
00:17:03,351 --> 00:17:06,020
You throw a pretty good line
for a guy who's out of practice.

315
00:17:07,438 --> 00:17:09,899
I'm doing all right, am I? Excellent.

316
00:17:11,943 --> 00:17:13,277
So what's with
the wedding ring?

317
00:17:14,445 --> 00:17:15,613
Oh, um...

318
00:17:18,324 --> 00:17:19,450
That's a long story.

319
00:17:20,618 --> 00:17:22,036
Maybe we should order
some drinks.

320
00:17:22,578 --> 00:17:23,621
Good idea.

321
00:17:24,997 --> 00:17:26,040
Excuse me.

322
00:17:38,511 --> 00:17:39,762
- Hey.
- Hey.

323
00:17:40,805 --> 00:17:41,847
Come.

324
00:17:47,436 --> 00:17:49,313
- Great minds.
- Right.

325
00:17:50,189 --> 00:17:51,899
So how's it going with Jane
and the girlfriend?

326
00:17:52,024 --> 00:17:54,235
Oh, it's a dead end,
if you ask me

327
00:17:54,485 --> 00:17:57,530
but Jane certainly seems
to be enjoying himself.

328
00:17:57,655 --> 00:17:59,198
He usually does.

329
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:02,451
Hello. From the gentlemen
at the bar.

330
00:18:02,868 --> 00:18:05,037
- Oh.
- Oh, boy.

331
00:18:05,913 --> 00:18:08,124
Oh, those gentlemen?
Oh, great. They're coming.

332
00:18:08,666 --> 00:18:10,001
Okay. Oh.

333
00:18:11,085 --> 00:18:12,128
Hello, ladies.

334
00:18:12,795 --> 00:18:14,714
I'm Dale. This is Mike.

335
00:18:16,591 --> 00:18:17,633
Hi.

336
00:18:18,259 --> 00:18:20,303
- I'm Kim.
- I'm Teresa.

337
00:18:20,678 --> 00:18:23,389
- Teresa. Beautiful name.
- Thank you.

338
00:18:23,598 --> 00:18:25,933
Are you two in town for
the orthodontics conference?

339
00:18:26,475 --> 00:18:30,229
- Oh. Uh, no.
- No. No. We're... we're cops.

340
00:18:31,439 --> 00:18:32,481
You're kidding.

341
00:18:33,691 --> 00:18:36,152
No, uh, actually, we're FBI.

342
00:18:36,402 --> 00:18:37,445
Oh.

343
00:18:39,322 --> 00:18:40,364
Cool.

344
00:18:40,906 --> 00:18:43,492
Well, it was nice to meet you.

345
00:18:43,826 --> 00:18:45,202
- Have a nice night.
- Hm.

346
00:18:46,454 --> 00:18:48,581
- Thank you.
- Never fails.

347
00:18:50,625 --> 00:18:52,376
Dale. Oh.

348
00:18:53,711 --> 00:18:54,754
That reminds me.

349
00:18:57,381 --> 00:18:58,883
- What is it?
- It's your badge.

350
00:18:59,675 --> 00:19:00,843
District sent it to me today.

351
00:19:02,011 --> 00:19:03,054
Congratulations.

352
00:19:04,889 --> 00:19:06,766
- You look surprised.
- No. I...

353
00:19:06,891 --> 00:19:08,601
Yeah, I just... I guess
it didn't feel real.

354
00:19:08,726 --> 00:19:10,186
Now it's... It's real.

355
00:19:11,312 --> 00:19:12,938
- I'm in the F.B.I.
- Welcome.

356
00:19:14,023 --> 00:19:15,066
Thank you.

357
00:19:17,068 --> 00:19:18,110
Oh, my God.

358
00:19:18,986 --> 00:19:21,030
Oh, my God, that's the craziest
story I've ever heard.

359
00:19:21,197 --> 00:19:22,365
- You killed him?
- Mm.

360
00:19:23,616 --> 00:19:25,451
That explains why you still
wear your wedding ring.

361
00:19:26,410 --> 00:19:27,495
Hm. I guess.

362
00:19:28,537 --> 00:19:30,623
You poor man.
What you've been through?

363
00:19:31,332 --> 00:19:32,667
I can't imagine.

364
00:19:33,417 --> 00:19:35,586
Well, you've been through
some tough times yourself.

365
00:19:36,462 --> 00:19:37,588
Mm, nah, nothing like that.

366
00:19:39,924 --> 00:19:41,634
I don't buy the tough girl act.

367
00:19:43,886 --> 00:19:44,929
I think...

368
00:19:46,097 --> 00:19:47,765
you cared about Vargas a lot

369
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:51,477
and it hurt you deeply
when he was killed.

370
00:19:52,311 --> 00:19:53,354
Sure, it hurt.

371
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:56,732
Well, loss has its way
of paralyzing you. It...

372
00:19:58,234 --> 00:20:00,486
It stops you from moving on
in your life

373
00:20:00,611 --> 00:20:04,907
and as hard as that is
and as guilty as you feel, it's...

374
00:20:05,825 --> 00:20:09,120
That's what you have to do.
Move on.

375
00:20:12,707 --> 00:20:14,083
That's what
I'm trying to do, anyhow.

376
00:20:15,710 --> 00:20:16,752
Trying.

377
00:20:20,548 --> 00:20:22,383
And this investigation
of yours.

378
00:20:23,175 --> 00:20:24,844
- Is it important?
- Yes.

379
00:20:25,678 --> 00:20:29,348
- To you, I mean?
- Yes.

380
00:20:31,892 --> 00:20:32,935
Maybe I can help.

381
00:20:34,103 --> 00:20:35,479
I thought you didn't know anything.

382
00:20:39,108 --> 00:20:40,234
"You lied to us, Miss Markham."

383
00:20:40,776 --> 00:20:43,154
I didn't want to withhold information

384
00:20:43,279 --> 00:20:46,323
but you have to understand,
I can't get involved in all this.

385
00:20:47,199 --> 00:20:49,577
- And now you can?
- Well, what can I say?

386
00:20:50,161 --> 00:20:51,412
Someone changed my mind.

387
00:20:52,329 --> 00:20:53,706
What can you tell us
about Paco Perez?

388
00:20:54,582 --> 00:20:57,543
He has a condo that he uses
by the beach.

389
00:20:57,668 --> 00:21:00,171
Uh, Richie and I went there
to party a couple times.

390
00:21:00,796 --> 00:21:02,590
- Do you know the address?
Oh, yeah, uh

391
00:21:02,715 --> 00:21:07,094
2014 Ocean something.
It's, it's right on the water.

392
00:21:08,137 --> 00:21:09,889
Is there anything else
you can tell us about Perez?

393
00:21:10,264 --> 00:21:12,808
Just that he'd probably kill me
if he knew I was talking to you.

394
00:21:13,267 --> 00:21:14,310
Has he threatened you before?

395
00:21:15,102 --> 00:21:17,730
No. But he's a violent man.

396
00:21:20,232 --> 00:21:23,652
Are you sure that this is safe?
That I'm safe?

397
00:21:23,861 --> 00:21:25,988
You have nothing to worry
about, Miss Markham.

398
00:21:26,322 --> 00:21:28,991
No one outside this room will ever
find out you cooperated with us.

399
00:21:30,618 --> 00:21:31,660
Trust me.

400
00:21:49,845 --> 00:21:51,889
- Any luck?
- Perez was definitely living here

401
00:21:52,014 --> 00:21:53,474
but no sign of him
when we arrived.

402
00:21:53,933 --> 00:21:54,975
You think he knew
we were coming?

403
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,894
Uh, it's hard to say, but it looks
like he left in a hurry.

404
00:21:57,019 --> 00:21:58,062
TV was still on.

405
00:21:58,395 --> 00:21:59,980
The condo building
has security cameras.

406
00:22:00,105 --> 00:22:01,232
See if you can pull the footage.

407
00:22:01,357 --> 00:22:02,608
We might able to see what car
he was driving

408
00:22:02,733 --> 00:22:03,776
or if he left with anyone.

409
00:22:03,901 --> 00:22:04,985
- We're on it.
- All right.

410
00:22:08,447 --> 00:22:09,490
All right.
Phones, computers

411
00:22:09,615 --> 00:22:11,450
any sig intel we can use
to trace Perez.

412
00:22:11,575 --> 00:22:13,327
I want all of it.
And he has a head start

413
00:22:13,452 --> 00:22:14,662
so let's move.
Clock's ticking.

414
00:22:28,551 --> 00:22:31,428
- Thanks again for the ride.
- Oh, it's my pleasure.

415
00:22:32,596 --> 00:22:33,639
Can I walk you in?

416
00:22:34,348 --> 00:22:37,560
Uh, if you walk me in,
I might invite you in

417
00:22:37,768 --> 00:22:40,020
and we both know
where that would lead.

418
00:22:42,773 --> 00:22:45,568
- Oh, you're trouble.
- Harmless as a fly.

419
00:22:46,569 --> 00:22:48,779
That makes me the spider.
I don't know how I feel about that.

420
00:22:48,988 --> 00:22:50,239
Right at home, I imagine.

421
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:54,451
- Next time. Okay?
- So there's a next time?

422
00:22:55,035 --> 00:22:57,454
If you want,
and if you call me.

423
00:22:59,123 --> 00:23:00,165
You know what I mean.

424
00:23:01,834 --> 00:23:03,335
Tomorrow. I'll call you tomorrow.

425
00:23:03,961 --> 00:23:05,004
Good.

426
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:13,971
- Bye.
- Bye.

427
00:23:26,233 --> 00:23:27,276
"Where have you been?"

428
00:23:37,953 --> 00:23:39,121
What are you doing here, Paco?

429
00:23:40,122 --> 00:23:41,248
I had nowhere else to go.

430
00:23:42,583 --> 00:23:45,127
The FBI just raided my place.

431
00:23:45,711 --> 00:23:47,171
Okay, that doesn't
answer my question.

432
00:23:47,296 --> 00:23:49,882
Why are you here
in my house?

433
00:23:50,007 --> 00:23:51,383
I think you know why I am here.

434
00:23:51,884 --> 00:23:54,470
I think you sent the FBI
to my condo.

435
00:23:54,929 --> 00:23:58,098
I think you wanted them
to find me and to arrest me.

436
00:23:59,141 --> 00:24:00,184
I don't know what you're
talking about.

437
00:24:00,309 --> 00:24:01,352
Enough!

438
00:24:05,648 --> 00:24:07,149
You know who I work for.

439
00:24:08,108 --> 00:24:10,611
You know what they would do
when they find out

440
00:24:10,736 --> 00:24:12,529
that you ratted me out
to the feds.

441
00:24:13,614 --> 00:24:14,823
And you know what I would do.

442
00:24:16,533 --> 00:24:19,036
Don't you ever threaten me,
you little bitch.

443
00:24:20,079 --> 00:24:21,538
Did you forget
who you're talking to?

444
00:24:21,747 --> 00:24:24,500
I run this town. I'm the boss.
Show some respect.

445
00:24:31,715 --> 00:24:32,758
Now.

446
00:24:34,927 --> 00:24:35,970
Let's start over.

447
00:24:38,722 --> 00:24:40,349
Why would I talk
to the FBI?

448
00:24:40,766 --> 00:24:42,518
Don't, don't, don't play dumb!

449
00:24:43,227 --> 00:24:44,269
With me out of the way,

450
00:24:44,395 --> 00:24:46,230
you have a straight line
to the Espedes cartel.

451
00:24:47,064 --> 00:24:49,149
But you just can't take me out.

452
00:24:50,067 --> 00:24:53,988
Otherwise, Colombia? Gone.
Your product? Gone.

453
00:24:54,113 --> 00:24:55,906
You? Gone.

454
00:24:57,157 --> 00:25:01,620
So this little game you are playing with
the FBI, it's not gonna work.

455
00:25:03,122 --> 00:25:05,207
Yes, it is.

456
00:25:06,417 --> 00:25:08,669
Five DEA agents are dead

457
00:25:09,044 --> 00:25:11,505
and the FBI thinks
that you killed them.

458
00:25:12,381 --> 00:25:14,049
I mean, I may not be able
to touch you

459
00:25:14,174 --> 00:25:17,594
but what if I made it look
like someone else did?

460
00:25:18,887 --> 00:25:21,682
Oh, you never thought of that?

461
00:25:24,101 --> 00:25:26,603
Relax. Paco.

462
00:25:30,983 --> 00:25:32,359
Uh, if I wanted to kill you...

463
00:25:35,779 --> 00:25:36,822
You'd be dead.

464
00:25:43,245 --> 00:25:44,329
Don't worry.
I'm not gonna kill you.

465
00:25:45,247 --> 00:25:46,290
Not now, anyway.

466
00:26:27,664 --> 00:26:29,416
"I thought you were gonna
call me tomorrow."

467
00:26:30,042 --> 00:26:32,795
It's tomorrow somewhere.
Bali, I think.

468
00:26:34,046 --> 00:26:35,089
It's a problem?

469
00:26:35,214 --> 00:26:38,509
No. No problem.
I'm just surprised.

470
00:26:39,259 --> 00:26:40,969
It happens so rarely these days.

471
00:26:42,137 --> 00:26:43,806
"I'm calling because I wanna
see you tomorrow."

472
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:45,682
"You're free?"

473
00:26:46,975 --> 00:26:50,938
Mm. I have some errands to run
and some things to take care of

474
00:26:51,063 --> 00:26:53,482
but I should be free
in the evening.

475
00:26:53,941 --> 00:26:54,983
It's a date.

476
00:26:58,821 --> 00:27:01,198
- Good night, Patrick.
- Good night, Krystal.

477
00:27:13,542 --> 00:27:14,835
We have a BOLO out on Perez.

478
00:27:14,960 --> 00:27:16,670
Corpus Christi PD's gonna
help with the search.

479
00:27:17,212 --> 00:27:18,255
What's this?

480
00:27:18,380 --> 00:27:20,382
Security camera footage
from Perez's apartment building.

481
00:27:20,507 --> 00:27:22,175
- You got anything?
- Not yet.

482
00:27:22,300 --> 00:27:23,844
The camera only catches
the front of the building

483
00:27:23,969 --> 00:27:25,262
so Perez could have
come and gone

484
00:27:25,387 --> 00:27:26,680
without us even knowing about it.

485
00:27:26,805 --> 00:27:29,558
Ladies, quick question. Huh?
Which shirt do I wear?

486
00:27:29,766 --> 00:27:31,184
Jane, we're kinda in the middle
of something right now.

487
00:27:31,309 --> 00:27:33,270
Please, I need the help.
It'll only take a second.

488
00:27:34,604 --> 00:27:36,481
Huh? Which one?
Uh this or this?

489
00:27:38,900 --> 00:27:41,027
- Are you sure?
- It's... Fine, that one.

490
00:27:41,236 --> 00:27:42,279
Eh.

491
00:27:43,113 --> 00:27:45,323
Jane, really? Come on.
We're trying to track down Perez.

492
00:27:45,448 --> 00:27:47,659
Are you gonna actually help with
this investigation, or what?

493
00:27:47,784 --> 00:27:48,827
Well, who says I'm not?

494
00:27:48,952 --> 00:27:51,329
Oh, you're helping
by going on a date.

495
00:27:51,454 --> 00:27:52,789
Well, it paid off once, didn't it?

496
00:27:52,914 --> 00:27:54,332
By the way, thank you
very much for the couch.

497
00:27:54,457 --> 00:27:56,042
Warms the place up tremendously.

498
00:27:58,837 --> 00:28:00,505
He is up to something
with that woman.

499
00:28:00,755 --> 00:28:03,133
- Yeah, I'll say.
- No. I mean he knows something

500
00:28:03,258 --> 00:28:04,384
that he's not telling us.

501
00:28:04,509 --> 00:28:06,052
I've seen it a thousand times.

502
00:28:06,261 --> 00:28:08,054
I don't know. He seemed
pretty interested in her.

503
00:28:08,263 --> 00:28:10,473
- She's not even his type.
- That's what I said.

504
00:28:10,974 --> 00:28:13,643
- What is his type?
- I don't know.

505
00:28:17,189 --> 00:28:18,231
Uh, this is a dead end.

506
00:28:19,107 --> 00:28:21,109
Uh, maybe Perez knew
about the cameras.

507
00:28:21,276 --> 00:28:23,111
- It was worth a try.
- You're right.

508
00:28:23,904 --> 00:28:26,364
At the DEA's office,
the gunmen knew

509
00:28:26,489 --> 00:28:28,742
about two of the hidden
security cameras.

510
00:28:28,867 --> 00:28:30,994
- Right.
- But not the third. Why?

511
00:28:31,828 --> 00:28:34,164
- Bad intel?
- Maybe, but even so

512
00:28:34,289 --> 00:28:35,415
where did the intel come from?

513
00:28:35,665 --> 00:28:37,876
How did they find out about
the two hidden security cameras

514
00:28:38,001 --> 00:28:39,836
- in the first place?
- I don't know.

515
00:28:40,712 --> 00:28:43,215
But I do know
where we can find out.

516
00:28:46,468 --> 00:28:47,552
Hello, Patrick.

517
00:28:48,511 --> 00:28:51,223
Hi. Uh, just wanted to make sure
we're still on for tonight.

518
00:28:52,265 --> 00:28:53,975
Mm, I'm looking forward to it.

519
00:28:54,684 --> 00:28:56,186
Uh, do you want to come
by the house?

520
00:28:56,311 --> 00:28:57,687
Love to. What time?

521
00:28:58,939 --> 00:29:00,398
- Let's say 7:00.
- I'll see you then.

522
00:29:01,650 --> 00:29:02,692
Bye.

523
00:29:06,905 --> 00:29:07,948
Comfy?

524
00:29:08,073 --> 00:29:09,282
Don't worry.
It'll be a short ride.

525
00:29:12,744 --> 00:29:14,329
So who knew about
the hidden cameras?

526
00:29:14,621 --> 00:29:15,664
Me.

527
00:29:16,748 --> 00:29:18,667
- My colleagues.
- And the gunmen.

528
00:29:18,917 --> 00:29:20,460
Somebody told them. Who?

529
00:29:20,710 --> 00:29:22,712
Maybe someone from
the cleaning crews.

530
00:29:23,338 --> 00:29:25,006
One of the techs
that installed the cameras.

531
00:29:25,423 --> 00:29:27,342
Drug ring could have bought off
any number of people.

532
00:29:27,968 --> 00:29:30,845
Look, what I do know is that
no one on my team would do this.

533
00:29:32,597 --> 00:29:35,058
Pull up a seat.
It's gonna take a while to download.

534
00:29:43,066 --> 00:29:44,734
You should have thought
things through, Paco.

535
00:29:46,695 --> 00:29:47,779
You should have been smarter.

536
00:29:51,366 --> 00:29:55,829
Ah, but then, you are a man.

537
00:29:59,124 --> 00:30:01,376
"Corpus Christi police department.
How can I help you?"

538
00:30:01,751 --> 00:30:03,753
Yes. I think I saw
the man on the news

539
00:30:03,878 --> 00:30:05,964
that you're looking for,
Paco Perez?

540
00:30:06,423 --> 00:30:07,465
"Where did you see him?"

541
00:30:07,799 --> 00:30:10,260
Uh, heading into an empty
house in my neighborhood.

542
00:30:10,385 --> 00:30:12,595
I thought it was strange because the
house has been empty for months.

543
00:30:13,054 --> 00:30:14,139
"What's the address, ma'am?"

544
00:30:14,848 --> 00:30:17,726
945 Clinton Street.

545
00:30:18,685 --> 00:30:20,061
"I have officers responding."

546
00:30:20,562 --> 00:30:22,355
"If you see him, do not
approach him on your own."

547
00:30:22,480 --> 00:30:24,607
- "Understand?"
- Yes, of course.

548
00:30:24,899 --> 00:30:25,942
"What's your name?"

549
00:30:35,618 --> 00:30:36,828
Sorry to have to run.

550
00:30:37,370 --> 00:30:41,249
I will kill you.
You hear me, bitch?

551
00:30:41,958 --> 00:30:43,001
I'll kill you!

552
00:30:45,045 --> 00:30:46,087
Goodbye, Paco.

553
00:30:50,675 --> 00:30:51,885
You know what to do. Just...

554
00:30:53,428 --> 00:30:54,471
Text me when you're done.

555
00:32:02,664 --> 00:32:04,124
Down. Down, down,
down, down!

556
00:32:10,004 --> 00:32:11,297
Cease fire. Cease fire.
Cease fire.

557
00:32:13,007 --> 00:32:15,635
- Jackson, Salazar, with me.
- Cover!

558
00:33:24,245 --> 00:33:25,288
What's up, Cho?

559
00:33:25,413 --> 00:33:27,290
- We found Perez. He's dead.
- What happened?

560
00:33:27,457 --> 00:33:29,667
Well, it looks like he opened
fire on Corpus Christi PD.

561
00:33:29,792 --> 00:33:31,628
The officers fired back.
They had more guns.

562
00:33:31,920 --> 00:33:33,213
Well, did we get anything
from the scene?

563
00:33:33,588 --> 00:33:35,465
A revolver.
All six rounds were fired.

564
00:33:35,590 --> 00:33:36,883
But there's something strange.

565
00:33:37,008 --> 00:33:39,177
I found a bullet hole in one of
the window frames of the house.

566
00:33:39,969 --> 00:33:42,096
- So?
- Well, it was at the back of the house

567
00:33:42,222 --> 00:33:43,890
which means someone
was shooting from the backyard.

568
00:33:44,015 --> 00:33:46,226
- I don't think Perez was alone.
- Thanks.

569
00:33:56,277 --> 00:33:58,238
- Is that...
- Krystal Markham.

570
00:33:59,113 --> 00:34:00,990
Higgins had said his colleagues
had interviewed her

571
00:34:01,115 --> 00:34:02,450
but that's not what
interested me.

572
00:34:03,201 --> 00:34:04,244
Watch this.

573
00:34:08,164 --> 00:34:11,334
She's looking into the camera,
like she knew it was there.

574
00:34:12,585 --> 00:34:13,628
I think she did.

575
00:34:17,632 --> 00:34:20,218
These are beautiful.
Thank you.

576
00:34:20,343 --> 00:34:22,804
- It's a little old-fashioned.
- I love them.

577
00:34:26,933 --> 00:34:27,976
Go take a seat.

578
00:34:28,226 --> 00:34:29,477
- I'll put these in water.
- Okay.

579
00:34:39,779 --> 00:34:40,947
- Hi.
- "Krystal..."

580
00:34:41,322 --> 00:34:42,782
I am right
in the middle of something.

581
00:34:42,949 --> 00:34:43,992
Call me back a little later.

582
00:34:44,617 --> 00:34:47,120
Krystal Markham
is the ringleader. Jane?

583
00:34:47,662 --> 00:34:48,746
Damn, he hung up.

584
00:35:00,341 --> 00:35:03,636
I thought we could have
a drink down by the water.

585
00:35:03,761 --> 00:35:05,513
My friend has a boat
he lets me use.

586
00:35:05,763 --> 00:35:07,432
- What do you say?
- Sounds wonderful.

587
00:35:08,016 --> 00:35:09,058
All right.

588
00:35:26,365 --> 00:35:29,285
Your friend lets you borrow this?

589
00:35:29,535 --> 00:35:32,455
Mm-hmm. He doesn't get a chance
to use it very much anymore.

590
00:35:33,164 --> 00:35:35,416
- Isn't he generous?
- Wow, some friend.

591
00:35:36,083 --> 00:35:37,126
Should I be jealous?

592
00:35:39,211 --> 00:35:40,254
Always.

593
00:35:49,847 --> 00:35:50,890
Thank you.

594
00:36:08,574 --> 00:36:10,076
How's your investigation coming?

595
00:36:10,201 --> 00:36:11,494
Oh, we've had some breakthroughs.

596
00:36:11,619 --> 00:36:13,621
We found Paco Perez,
thanks to you.

597
00:36:14,121 --> 00:36:15,915
Oh? Is he in custody?

598
00:36:16,791 --> 00:36:18,417
No, uh, dead.

599
00:36:19,377 --> 00:36:20,920
Corpus Christi police
shot him dead.

600
00:36:21,045 --> 00:36:23,214
Well, at least that's what
they think happened.

601
00:36:23,506 --> 00:36:24,548
And you?

602
00:36:24,882 --> 00:36:27,134
Oh, I like to keep an open mind.

603
00:36:27,718 --> 00:36:28,803
I like that about you.

604
00:36:32,807 --> 00:36:33,849
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

605
00:36:37,853 --> 00:36:39,355
Now that Paco is dead

606
00:36:39,563 --> 00:36:41,273
I imagine you'll be heading
back to Austin.

607
00:36:42,149 --> 00:36:43,192
In due time.

608
00:36:45,403 --> 00:36:47,446
- What's keeping you here?
- You are.

609
00:36:52,243 --> 00:36:53,285
Sorry.

610
00:36:53,786 --> 00:36:54,829
Excuse me.

611
00:36:55,496 --> 00:36:56,539
So rude.

612
00:37:01,085 --> 00:37:02,128
You're a wanted man.

613
00:37:02,253 --> 00:37:03,629
Maybe I'm the one
who should be jealous.

614
00:37:03,796 --> 00:37:05,297
It's just work.
Nothing important.

615
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:08,884
Well, personally, I hope your
investigation drags on for weeks.

616
00:37:09,051 --> 00:37:10,094
And why is that?

617
00:37:10,553 --> 00:37:12,012
You and I are getting
to know each other.

618
00:37:12,555 --> 00:37:16,308
Well, sadly, I don't think
it's gonna go on much longer.

619
00:37:16,767 --> 00:37:17,810
I have a new theory.

620
00:37:19,228 --> 00:37:21,480
- Can you share it with me?
- Sure. I trust you.

621
00:37:22,606 --> 00:37:24,817
First thing that stuck out to me
was that the gunmen

622
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:28,738
knew of two of the hidden
cameras, but not a third.

623
00:37:29,655 --> 00:37:30,698
Didn't make sense.

624
00:37:31,449 --> 00:37:33,409
Unless, of course, the person
that sent the gunmen in

625
00:37:33,534 --> 00:37:34,869
wanted them to be caught.

626
00:37:35,661 --> 00:37:36,954
- Clever.
- Yeah, it is.

627
00:37:37,496 --> 00:37:40,166
- And the second thing?
- Well, it's just a theory, like I said

628
00:37:40,291 --> 00:37:42,960
but this Mr. X that the DEA
keeps talking about.

629
00:37:43,085 --> 00:37:46,005
We know he's disciplined,
he's organized, he's careful.

630
00:37:46,630 --> 00:37:49,508
- And smart.
- But?

631
00:37:49,633 --> 00:37:52,970
But here's a man that runs
this huge drug ring.

632
00:37:53,095 --> 00:37:55,514
And doesn't just run it.
He runs it seamlessly.

633
00:37:56,182 --> 00:37:57,641
And yet no one knows
who he is.

634
00:37:59,018 --> 00:38:01,395
He's a man that's completely
void of ego.

635
00:38:01,562 --> 00:38:04,190
And in all my life,
I don't know that I've ever met a man

636
00:38:04,315 --> 00:38:05,357
who could do that.

637
00:38:05,649 --> 00:38:10,362
A man who would completely
shun all attention?

638
00:38:11,197 --> 00:38:12,698
That just got me thinking, and...

639
00:38:13,282 --> 00:38:16,744
Well, you know, maybe this Mr. X
is a woman.

640
00:38:18,204 --> 00:38:20,664
- That's quite an interesting theory.
- Yeah, I think so.

641
00:38:21,916 --> 00:38:22,958
I'm not loving this.

642
00:38:23,542 --> 00:38:24,710
I think I'm gonna open
another bottle.

643
00:38:25,628 --> 00:38:26,670
Oh.

644
00:38:40,643 --> 00:38:41,685
I like it.

645
00:38:42,436 --> 00:38:43,562
I'm curious about something.

646
00:38:43,687 --> 00:38:46,315
And, and don't worry
if you can't answer this.

647
00:38:46,524 --> 00:38:47,566
I won't.

648
00:38:49,443 --> 00:38:51,946
This woman.
Who do you think she is?

649
00:38:55,699 --> 00:38:56,742
You.

650
00:39:05,626 --> 00:39:07,795
- Well, what makes you say that?
- You're smart.

651
00:39:08,838 --> 00:39:11,799
Smart enough to let people
think that you're not.

652
00:39:12,591 --> 00:39:14,051
Which is exactly the trait

653
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:17,555
that allowed Mr. X to be
a mystery for all these years.

654
00:39:18,222 --> 00:39:19,807
Besides, I knew better
than to think

655
00:39:19,932 --> 00:39:21,767
that you were interested
in me, because

656
00:39:22,643 --> 00:39:25,187
well, you were interested in me.

657
00:39:28,691 --> 00:39:31,193
- You underestimate yourself.
- Not this time.

658
00:39:31,402 --> 00:39:33,779
Well, I guess we'll never know.

659
00:39:34,697 --> 00:39:35,739
Hm.

660
00:39:36,198 --> 00:39:37,241
A question. If I...

661
00:39:37,533 --> 00:39:40,536
If I am so capable,
So smart, as you say

662
00:39:41,871 --> 00:39:43,998
how did I end up here?
Where did I go wrong?

663
00:39:44,248 --> 00:39:47,877
It wasn't anything you did.
You were flawless. Really.

664
00:39:48,294 --> 00:39:50,379
And the way you set
the gunmen up to be caught

665
00:39:50,629 --> 00:39:53,215
and killing them, and linking
the murder to Perez

666
00:39:53,340 --> 00:39:57,636
and having Perez killed the way you did,
my particular favorite.

667
00:39:57,761 --> 00:40:00,806
I mean, the Corpus Christi police
probably still think that they shot him.

668
00:40:04,101 --> 00:40:05,519
You're wrong about
one thing, Patrick.

669
00:40:07,062 --> 00:40:08,898
I didn't have Paco killed.

670
00:40:10,065 --> 00:40:11,233
I shot him myself.

671
00:40:14,028 --> 00:40:15,070
My mistake.

672
00:40:17,281 --> 00:40:19,742
Yes, it is.

673
00:40:22,995 --> 00:40:24,663
If you shoot me,
you'll be caught.

674
00:40:24,830 --> 00:40:26,582
Look around, Patrick.
No witnesses.

675
00:40:27,207 --> 00:40:28,250
No.

676
00:40:30,377 --> 00:40:31,420
But...

677
00:40:33,339 --> 00:40:34,590
the FBI...

678
00:40:37,092 --> 00:40:39,386
has been listening
to everything you've said.

679
00:40:40,721 --> 00:40:42,181
And they will be arriving...

680
00:40:43,849 --> 00:40:45,559
right about...

681
00:40:48,646 --> 00:40:49,688
Now.

682
00:40:57,321 --> 00:40:58,364
Now.

683
00:41:01,659 --> 00:41:02,701
Now.

684
00:41:03,118 --> 00:41:04,161
Nice try.

685
00:41:14,630 --> 00:41:17,132
This is the F.B.I.
Drop your weapon now.

686
00:41:40,531 --> 00:41:41,573
Bye.

687
00:41:44,576 --> 00:41:47,788
- Jane? You okay?
- Oh, I'm fine. Barely.

688
00:41:48,747 --> 00:41:50,207
You guys took your time
getting here, didn't you?

689
00:41:50,332 --> 00:41:51,458
Another minute,
I would have been...

690
00:41:52,459 --> 00:41:55,379
bobbing around there
in the marina like a, a dead duck.

691
00:41:55,754 --> 00:41:58,674
- Maybe you'll learn your lesson.
- Wh..., what lesson is that?

692
00:41:58,882 --> 00:42:01,468
If you'd actually told us about
your plan in advance

693
00:42:01,593 --> 00:42:02,761
we'd have had time to get here.

694
00:42:02,886 --> 00:42:04,763
I've been trying to tell him
that for years.

695
00:42:04,888 --> 00:42:06,515
Oh, Cho, you're with me,
aren't you?

696
00:42:06,640 --> 00:42:08,684
No, I'm with them.
You're a terrible communicator.

697
00:42:08,809 --> 00:42:10,185
You're just lucky we found
the right boat.

698
00:42:12,396 --> 00:42:13,439
Okay, well, yeah

699
00:42:13,564 --> 00:42:15,524
maybe I need to work
on my communication skills.

700
00:42:16,108 --> 00:42:18,444
But, you know, no problem.
Thanks for solving the crime

701
00:42:18,902 --> 00:42:20,863
and just a little hypothermia.
I'll get over it.

702
00:42:22,031 --> 00:42:23,073
Whew!

